&gt;&gt; AND THEN CAME CHANGE.

00:06:23.332 --> 00:06:25.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:06:23.799 --> 00:06:27.770
&gt;&gt; Laura: I MEAN, A.B., YOU

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:28.804
SAT NEXT TO HIM ON SO MANY

00:06:27.903 --> 00:06:30.005
EVENINGS.

00:06:28.937 --> 00:06:32.041
&gt;&gt; JUST BRILLIANT.

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:33.609
I WROTE ABOUT HIM LAST WEEKEND I

00:06:32.174 --> 00:06:36.145
SAID THAT THE ONLY DEBATE THAT I

00:06:33.742 --> 00:06:38.213
EVER WON IN NINE YEARS WAS ON

00:06:36.278 --> 00:06:39.181
THE SUPER COMMITTEE, WHICH WAS A

00:06:38.347 --> 00:06:41.383
DEBT CUTTING COMMITTEE, WHICH

00:06:39.314 --> 00:06:42.584
FELL FLAT ON ITS FACE, HE WROTE

00:06:41.517 --> 00:06:43.786
WITH GREAT HOPE ABOUT HOW IT ALL

00:06:42.718 --> 00:06:45.554
MIGHT WORK OUT.

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:46.789
IT WAS REALLY GOING TO BE A

00:06:45.687 --> 00:06:48.457
GREAT OPPORTUNITY.

00:06:46.922 --> 00:06:49.958
WHEN I BUSTED HIM ABOUT IT, WHEN

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:52.461
IT FOLDED, HE SAID THAT WAS ONE

00:06:50.092 --> 00:06:53.362
OF THE TIMES WHERE I WASN'T

00:06:52.594 --> 00:06:56.065
CYNICAL ENOUGH.

00:06:53.495 --> 00:06:58.400
HE WAS NEVER WRONG.

00:06:56.198 --> 00:06:59.201
HIS PREDICTION DIDN'T COME TRUE.

00:06:58.534 --> 00:07:00.769
USUALLY BECAUSE HE HASN'T BEEN

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:01.904
CYNICAL ENOUGH.

00:07:00.903 --> 00:07:04.907
BUT FOR SOMEONE WHO WAS SO

00:07:02.037 --> 00:07:07.876
CYNICAL, HE WAS ALSO ALWAYS FULL

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.978
OF HOPE AND JOY.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:12.614
AND HE REALLY DELIGHTED IN THE

00:07:10.112 --> 00:07:14.783
LITTLE THINGS, AND THAT WAS AN

00:07:12.748 --> 00:07:17.186
INCREDIBLE COMBINATION, SO

00:07:14.917 --> 00:07:18.420
STOIC, SO STRONG, BECAUSE OF HIS

00:07:17.319 --> 00:07:21.356
BATTLE, AND WHAT HE HAD TO

00:07:18.554 --> 00:07:23.058
SURMOUNT IN THE WAKE OF IT.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:25.360
BUT THEN, JUST AS SOMEONE WHO

00:07:23.192 --> 00:07:26.361
REALLY DELIGHTED IN THE WARMTH

00:07:25.494 --> 00:07:28.997
AND EXCHANGE OF PEOPLE.

00:07:26.495 --> 00:07:31.200
HE LOVED PEOPLE.

00:07:29.131 --> 00:07:32.367
WE HAD A NIGHT RIGHT HERE AT THE

00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:33.802
TABLE, I'LL NEVER FORGET, EARLY

00:07:32.501 --> 00:07:36.605
ON WHEN I DIDN'T KNOW HIM WELL,

00:07:33.936 --> 00:07:39.108
AND I WAS SEATED IN BETWEEN HIM

00:07:36.738 --> 00:07:39.842
AND STEVE AND BRET ARE MAKING

00:07:39.241 --> 00:07:44.179
SOME COLLEGE OVER DRINKING

00:07:39.975 --> 00:07:46.281
JOKES, AND CHARLES SAID, THAT

00:07:44.313 --> 00:07:47.716
COMMERCIAL ALWAYS SAYS TO ME,

00:07:46.415 --> 00:07:49.418
THE ONLY BEER TO HAVE WHEN YOU

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:51.220
ARE HAVING MORE THAN ONE.

00:07:49.551 --> 00:07:53.589
THEN HE PAUSED PERFECTLY TIMED,

00:07:51.353 --> 00:07:55.090
MORE THAN ONE WHAT?

00:07:53.722 --> 00:07:56.792
AND THEN OF COURSE, IT WAS RIGHT

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:58.594
BACK TO THE PANEL, AND WE WERE

00:07:56.925 --> 00:08:00.395
BACK ON CAMERA, AND I WAS

00:07:58.727 --> 00:08:01.830
PRACTICALLY UNDER THE TABLE.

00:08:00.529 --> 00:08:02.631
HIS COMEDIC TIMING WAS

00:08:01.964 --> 00:08:04.366
UNBELIEVABLE.

00:08:02.764 --> 00:08:05.701
ALSO, SOMETIMES, JUST HAD THE

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.002
DELIGHT OF A SMALL KID.

00:08:05.834 --> 00:08:07.336
IT WAS REALLY SOMETHING TO

00:08:07.136 --> 00:08:11.240
BEHOLD.

00:08:07.469 --> 00:08:12.608
&gt;&gt; Laura: PSYCHIATRIST,

00:08:11.373 --> 00:08:13.475
HARVARD MEDICAL SCHOOL, PULITZER

00:08:12.741 --> 00:08:13.842
PRIZE, MORE AWARDS THAN WE CAN

00:08:13.609 --> 00:08:17.546
LIST HERE.

00:08:13.976 --> 00:08:20.649
BUT CHARLES, WHEN HE WROTE ABOUT

00:08:17.679 --> 00:08:23.919
A POLITICAL MOVEMENT OR EVENT,

00:08:20.782 --> 00:08:26.188
HE WROTE ABOUT IT IN A WAY THAT

00:08:24.052 --> 00:08:28.824
HE CUT THROUGH WHERE SO MANY

00:08:26.321 --> 00:08:29.992
OTHERS WERE MIRED IN MINUTIA.

00:08:28.957 --> 00:08:30.993
PRESIDENT REAGAN, I LOVED THIS

